// The rate of change of a smoothed high to low range, which answers whether the
// bar is getting wider rather than how wide it is.
//
// Exercises: an exponential mean of a range rather than of a price, a rate of
// change taken over that mean, and the division that has no answer when a
// stretch of perfectly flat bars leaves nothing to compare against.

version 1

study("Volatility ratio", precision = 4)

periods  = input(10, "Periods", min = 1, max = 2000)
lookback = input(10, "Rate of change lookback", min = 1, max = 2000)

// An exponential mean rather than a simple one. A simple mean of ranges reacts
// to one wide bar for a whole window and then drops it in a single step, which
// prints a second move on the rate of change that the data never made.
smoothed = ema(high - low, periods)

level(0, "Zero", fade(silver, 60), style = "dashed")

plot(smoothed[lookback] == 0 ? none : 100 * (smoothed - smoothed[lookback]) / smoothed[lookback],
     "Ratio", purple, width = 2)
